  "query_preview": "..Storms have fired up across portions of our CWA,\nespecially in Yavapai and Coconino Counties where model guidance \nsuggests the strongest instability is. Sufficient moisture remains\nin place across the state as shown in our above normal PW values.\nAnother shortwave is the main culprit for today's activity. The\nsounding from this afternoon does show a decent cap, so storms \naren't very severe in nature, but that could change through the \nrest of the afternoon. For now, training storms leading to flash \nflooding seems to be the main concern. \n\nA broad trough across the West Coast will lead way to a handful of\nembedded shortwaves pushing through the state this week. This will\nkeep us in a rather activity pattern each day. Although guidance \nsuggests convection being rather widespread/heaviest during the \nafternoon periods, overnight activity could quickly downplay how \neach day turns out. Between the atmosphere being worked over and \nlikelihood of debris clouds, we could see quieter days than \nmodels are depicting at this time. As always, we'll do our best, \nbut in environments like this taking it day-by-day is usually the \nbest plan of attack. \n\nBy next weekend overall precipitation chances look to diminish,\nbut a few isolated showers across eastern Arizona may still\nremain in the forecast. More details on that later.",
